title: "pallet-delegated-staking: reject zero-amount delegations for new delegators"
doc:
  - audience: Runtime Dev
    description: |
      A zero `amount` no longer creates a `Delegation` record for an account that is not
      already a delegator. Previously such a call leaked a provider reference and permanently
      marked the account as a delegator, blocking it from registering as an agent.

      `delegate_to_agent` (via `do_delegate`) and `migrate_delegation` now fail with
      `InvalidDelegation` when the amount is zero and the delegator does not yet exist, and
      `Delegation::update` writes nothing for a new zero-amount entry, so no write path can
      persist one.

      A zero-amount top-up on an *existing* delegation stays a no-op and is deliberately not
      rejected: `pallet-nomination-pools`' `bond_extra(BondExtra::Rewards)` bonds a claimed
      amount of zero when nothing is pending, for example at 100% commission, and rejecting it
      would break reward bonding for those pools.

      A try-state check asserts that stored delegations are non-zero.
crates:
  - name: pallet-delegated-staking
    bump: patch
